<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8349" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-vādo</span></b> , vāsi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v.a.</i>, <i>to assail</i> or <i>attack
				on every side</i>, <i>to encompass</i>, <i>beset</i> (not ante-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					10, 2, 12</span></i>
			: aliquem clamoribus turbidis, * <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12,
				43</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">redeuntem noctu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 30, 48, § 92</span></i>
			. —<i>Pass.</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Amm. 20, 6,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, ofterror falling upon one (so only a
			few times in Liv.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">novus terror cum ex parte utrāque
					circumvasisset aciem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					9, 40, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">barbaros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					34, 21, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					34, 38, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
